course: dictionary
lesson: 7192
title: Pesach, a spring festival
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pesach is a Hebrew word, and it is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. The sentence tells you what it means: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival». The word «or» is a clue that the two names mean the same thing.
explain: Look at the words around Pesach for more clues. «Remembering the Exodus from Egypt» tells you the festival is about a story. Exodus means leaving, and it is the story of how God freed the Israelites from slavery in Egypt.
explain: The sentence also explains «matzah» for you: «a flat bread made without yeast». You do not need a dictionary when the writer tells you the meaning right inside the sentence. Always check whether your meaning still makes sense in the sentence.
fact: Pesach is the Hebrew name for Passover, a spring festival.
fact: Jewish people remember how God freed the Israelites from slavery in Egypt.
fact: The story is told in the Book of Exodus.
fact: Families hold a Seder meal, and they read the story from a book called the Haggadah.
fact: Matzah is a flat bread made without yeast, and it is eaten at the Seder meal.
exercise: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival.» What is another name for Passover? | *Pesach | Exodus | Haggadah | Matzah
exercise: When is Pesach celebrated? | Summer | Autumn | Winter | *Spring
exercise: What is matzah? | A sweet cake with yeast | A type of soup | *A flat bread made without yeast | A candle lit at the start of a meal
test: Which book is read from at the Seder meal? | Passover | Book of Exodus | *Haggadah | Matzah
test: What does Pesach remember? | *How God freed the Israelites from slavery in Egypt | How Egypt won a great war | How the spring rain came back | How a king built a city
exam: What is the English name for Pesach? | *Passover | Ramadan | Hanukkah | Diwali
